Shrink the from-source mbedTLS TLS record length 8 KB -> 6 KB.

The record buffer was sized (16 KB -> 8 KB, then here -> 6 KB) to hold the largest
control message. All large control frames (submit_map / submit_topology) are ALWAYS
chunked at the client (web/src/net/client.ts sendChunked; the fx_bench and map_upload
harnesses shard likewise), so no single record exceeds one base64-inflated chunk (a
4 KB window -> ~5.6 KB record) — comfortably under 6 KB. With
CONFIG_MBEDTLS_DYNAMIC_BUFFER the record buffer is allocated per-connection off the ssl
context sized to this cap, so the smaller cap shrinks that allocation (~8.7 KB -> ~6.7 KB
contiguous) — headroom that lets the heapless-netstack player serve many TLS connections
on the C6's tight, fragmentable heap instead of wedging after one. ABI-safe vs the
prebuilt esp-tls / esp_https_server (the length lives off the struct). Applied to the
pinned embedded archive via archive_override(patches=...) in //MODULE.bazel.

diff --git a/nix/mbedtls_src.BUILD b/nix/mbedtls_src.BUILD
--- a/nix/mbedtls_src.BUILD
+++ b/nix/mbedtls_src.BUILD
@@ -106,11 +106,11 @@
